  "observedImprovements": [
    "Actual connected source face is narrower and elongated, recentered on the body, with a stronger nasal bridge and bounded local lid/lip sculpt. Original ears/neck remain present in true3q/profile.",
    "Huge blank torso and four broad U-fold underlay have been integrated into varied hand-drawn oblique fan drapery, with short branch/tuck paths and a narrow chased cloth edge.",
    "Three sculpted neck rings, sleeve tension folds and smaller leg folds remain genuine connected 3D source surfaces in front/body3q/low views.",
    "Both source hands stay raised; high projecting palm/finger region and full original lower contact band retain exact positions.",
    "R03 stacked eye ridges and R04 excessively smoothed facial features were rejected and rolled back to a conservative blend."
  ],
  "remainingFailures": [
    "The face remains recognizably derived from the different Sainsbury artifact. Lids are still narrower and the mouth more youthful than the supplied calm rounded reference; likeness is unaccepted.",
    "Compact integrated curl relief now avoids long raised spiral worms, but still reads as beaded/engraved gold, with a visible two-tier source cap. It is not an accepted match to the fine reference curls.",
    "Oblique chest drapes are improved from the blank four-U-fold source, but fold/layer separation and the chased border do not reproduce all reference detail. Sleeve/leg cloth still differs.",
    "The source gold, native room lighting and all camera parameters remain195. This is not a test against root's independently updated floor200 or altar198 candidate.",
    "No self-intersection proof, physical export or final-film performance/likeness acceptance is established. Topology and finite normals are integrity facts, not photographic acceptance."
  ],
